# Without the trailing slash this also matches a *symlink* named
# node_modules. The slash form matches directories only, which is how an
# absolute, machine-specific symlink reached main in #173: agents and test
# runs routinely link node_modules into a scratch worktree, and `git add -A`
# then picks the link up because nothing ignores it.
node_modules
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data
dashboard/backend/data/
.openclaw-factory/
.openclaw-worktrees/

# Factory process artifacts — gate evidence, agent scratch, synthetic
# infra-failure notes. These belong to a task's run, never to the product,
# and must not be swept into a task branch by `git add -A` at publish time.
#
# Anchored to the worktree root, which is the only place a run writes them:
# openclaw-runner.mjs and objective/orchestrator.mjs both resolve
# <worktree>/evidence. Unanchored, this pattern also matched product source in
# any directory named evidence/ — `git add -A` then dropped it with no error,
# which is how the FCT-P0-05 modules were written, tested and left
# uncommittable. See factory/test/evidence-gitignore-scope.test.mjs.
/evidence/
/*-qa.test.log
/*-qa.exitcode
/*-qa.summary.md
/*.exitcode
agents/**/logs/*
agents/**/outputs/*
!agents/**/logs/.gitkeep
!agents/**/outputs/.gitkeep

# Local OpenClaw state and secrets should never be committed.
.openclaw/
openclaw.json
/IDENTITY.md
/SOUL.md
/USER.md
/MEMORY.md
credentials/
secrets/
memory/
tasks/
flows/
cron/
devices/
identity/
/.openclaw/logs/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
